From 357c20f6d6e8005c3d96434f1ad852284f0ea9e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:36:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] bcm2835-pwmaudiod: headphone jack of the Raspberry Pi 3
 as audiohw

Two PWM channels (GPIO 40 and 41, ALT0) with their clock from PLLD/2
(250 MHz, range 5669 at 44.1 kHz) play the jack. The DMA controller
(channel 2, if the devicetree mask leaves it free) feeds the PWM FIFO from
a ring of 8 slots of 512 frames; a 10 ms timer follows the ring, fills
played slots with silence and lets waiting writes in. Writes of exactly
2048 bytes as for ac97d, EWOULDBLOCK while the ring is full. The ring
starts with a 46 ms ramp to the middle against the click.

/scheme/audiohw/stats shows clock, range, measured rate and error
counters; writing seconds to /scheme/audiohw/tone plays a 1 kHz sine with
the CPU filling the FIFO (no DMA), as a test. Without a PWM block (QEMU)
the ring is played by the clock, so audiod and the scheme still run.

Refs redox-rpi/redox-rpi#250

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
